  "note": {
    "status": "draft",
    "text": "The Egyptians wrote numbers with pictures: a stroke for 1, a heel bone for 10, a coil of rope for 100 and a lotus flower for 1000. To read a number, add the values of all the pictures. So 3 lotus flowers and 2 heel bones make 3020. They had no place value, so they did not need a zero digit to hold empty places.\n\nThe Romans used seven letters: I = 1, V = 5, X = 10, L = 50, C = 100, D = 500 and M = 1000.\n• When a letter is followed by one of equal or smaller value, add: VI = 6, XX = 20.\n• When a smaller letter comes before a bigger one, subtract: IV = 4, IX = 9, XL = 40, XC = 90, CD = 400, CM = 900.\n• Never write the same letter more than three times in a row: write IV, not IIII.\n\nThis year, 2026, is MMXXVI.",
    "checks": [
      "3 * 1000 + 2 * 10 == 3020",
      "fromRoman('VI') == 6",
      "fromRoman('XX') == 20",
      "fromRoman('IV') == 4",
      "fromRoman('IX') == 9",
      "fromRoman('XL') == 40",
      "fromRoman('XC') == 90",
      "fromRoman('CD') == 400",
      "fromRoman('CM') == 900",
      "roman(2026) == 'MMXXVI'"
    ]
  },
  "worked_example": {
    "status": "draft",
    "vars": {
      "n": 1948,
      "th": {
        "expr": "idiv(n, 1000) * 1000"
      },
      "h": {
        "expr": "idiv(n, 100) % 10 * 100"
      },
      "t": {
        "expr": "idiv(n, 10) % 10 * 10"
      },
      "u": {
        "expr": "n % 10"
      }
    },
    "problem": "Ewane's grandmother was born in {str(n)}. Write the year {str(n)} in Roman numerals.",
    "steps": [
      "Split the number by place value: {str(n)} = {str(th)} + {h} + {t} + {u}.",
      "{str(th)} = {roman(th)}.",
      "{h} = {roman(h)}: C (one hundred) before M (one thousand) means one thousand minus one hundred.",
      "{t} = {roman(t)}: X (ten) before L (fifty) means fifty minus ten.",
      "{u} = {roman(u)}: V followed by three I's.",
      "Join the parts in order: {roman(th)} + {roman(h)} + {roman(t)} + {roman(u)}."
    ],
    "answer": "{str(n)} = {roman(n)}",
    "checks": [
      "th + h + t + u == n",
      "roman(th) + roman(h) + roman(t) + roman(u) == roman(n)",
      "fromRoman(roman(n)) == n",
      "roman(h) == 'CM' && roman(t) == 'XL'"
    ]
  },
